{"divisionId":3571,"date":"2026-03-12T00:00:00","number":1,"notes":null,"title":"Greenhouse Gas Emissions Trading Scheme (Amendment) (Extension to Maritime Activities) Order 2026","isWhipped":true,"isGovernmentContent":false,"authoritativeContentCount":26,"authoritativeNotContentCount":134,"divisionHadTellers":true,"tellerContentCount":26,"tellerNotContentCount":134,"memberContentCount":24,"memberNotContentCount":132,"sponsoringMemberId":210,"isHouse":true,"isInquorate":false,"amendmentMotionNotes":"<p>Baroness Hoey moved, as an amendment to the motion to approve the&nbsp; Order, to leave out all the words after \"that\" and insert \"this House declines to approve the draft Order laid before the House on 13 January because while the Scottish Islands are protected from the Order, Northern Ireland, which is already marginalised from the rest of the UK through the imposition of the Windsor Framework, is denied the same protection; and because in a context where no viable fuel alternatives exist the only impact of the Order will be to increase bureaucratic burdens on business and impose additional costs on those living in parts of the UK that depend on maritime transport.&rdquo; The House divided:</p>","isGovernmentWin":true,"remoteVotingStart":"2026-03-12T14:55:00","remoteVotingEnd":"2026-03-12T15:03:00","divisionWasExclusivelyRemote":false,"contentTellers":[{"memberId":655,"name":"Lord McCrea of Magherafelt and Cookstown","listAs":"McCrea of Magherafelt and Cookstown, L.","memberFrom":"Life peer","party":"Democratic Unionist Party","partyColour":"d46a4c","partyAbbreviation":"DUP","partyIsMainParty":false},{"memberId":4352,"name":"Lord Hay of Ballyore","listAs":"Hay of Ballyore, L.","memberFrom":"Life peer","party":"Democratic Unionist Party","partyColour":"d46a4c","partyAbbreviation":"DUP","partyIsMainParty":false}],"notContentTellers":[{"memberId":4508,"name":"Baroness Anderson of Stoke-on-Trent","listAs":"Anderson of Stoke-on-Trent, B.","memberFrom":"Life peer","par